==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAudit  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAudit.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AppendOnlyAudit removes the constraint that every audit row originated from a successful mutation operation. The injected fact forces an orphan audit row (no operation references it), which is exactly the configuration that append-only forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly, FR_018_AuditRetained
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditRetained: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_SuccessRequiresPermission  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_SuccessRequiresPermission.als
    rationale: Clearing F_SuccessRequiresPermission removes the (role, op) authorisation check. The injection constructs a Member-role caller who is not the owner of the target task yet successfully PATCHes it — exactly the privilege-escalation scenario FR-009 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_009_NonOwnerMemberCannotEdit, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_NonOwnerMemberCannotEdit: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Clearing F_CrossTeamIsolation removes the rule that a target task in another team must produce NotFound. The injection forces a successful GetTaskById against a task whose team differs from the caller's X-Team-Id, i.e. a cross-tenant leak.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_011_CrossTeamIsolation, FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuthRequired removes the rule that unauthenticated requests are rejected. The injection forces a Success outcome on an unauthenticated operation, violating FR-001.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditOnSuccessfulMutation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditOnSuccessfulMutation.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditOnSuccessfulMutation removes the obligation to write an audit entry on a successful mutation. The injection forces a successful PostTasks with no audit row, which is exactly the missing-audit scenario FR-015 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_OneAuditPerSave
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_OneAuditPerSave: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttributionCorrect  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttributionCorrect.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditAttributionCorrect removes the rule that the audit entry's actor equals the operation's caller. The injection forces an audit entry whose recorded actor differs from the caller — a misattribution.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_IdentityFromAuth
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_IdentityFromAuth: FAIL (expected)

